{"event_type":"move_chosen","payload":{"expected_effect":"New traffic will no longer be routed to target-b through the slow HAProxy path; all requests will go to target-a, which has normal latency (~0.03 s p95). The user-visible p95 latency and error rate will return to within limits. Target-b will be taken out of rotation while the path issue is examined.","move":"drain-worker target-b","reasoning":"Target-b is affected by a network_path fault: the worker is healthy when reached directly, but the path through HAProxy is slow (p95 ~1.6 s vs. limit 0.5 s). This fault class is defined as 'the worker behaves normally when reached directly but not through the entry point', and software cannot repair the network path. The only software action that mitigates this without requiring the faulty path is to stop routing new traffic to target-b. Target-a is healthy and can serve all traffic. Draining target-b first satisfies the 'refused if no other worker is serving' guard because target-a remains in rotation.","risk":"Target-b loses capacity and its requests will queue or fail until it is undrained or repaired. Since target-a is healthy and serving, no overall service outage occurs. The drain is reversible with undrain-worker once the path is fixed."},"run_id":"run-754547a3","sequence":31,"timestamp":"2026-10-18T08:17:02.111612+00:00"}
